<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="39572" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MATH/595/39572.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="MATH" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MATH.xml">Mathematics</subject><course id="595" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MATH/595.xml">Advanced Topics in Mathematics</course></parents><sectionNumber>EK </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Floer Theory With Applications</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic:  Floer Theory With Applications. In this class we will study the definition and construction of Hamiltonian and Lagrangian Floer theory. We will then explore applications of these tools to Hamiltonian dynamics, symplectic embedding obstructions and the relations of Floer theory to Gromov-Witten theory and the topology of loop spaces.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Not intended for Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>242</roomNumber><buildingName>Armory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Kerman" firstName="E">Kerman, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>